The extension is built on ext-php-rs (https://github.com/extphprs/ext-php-rs, MIT OR Apache-2.0),
used as a dependency for the Zend Engine bindings, zval ownership and module plumbing.

SCRAM authentication uses, as dependencies (all MIT OR Apache-2.0, pure Rust): the RustCrypto
crates sha1, sha2, md-5, hmac and pbkdf2 (https://github.com/RustCrypto), getrandom
(https://github.com/rust-random/getrandom) and unicode-normalization
(https://github.com/unicode-rs/unicode-normalization). The SASLprep tables in
crates/core/src/auth/tables.rs are libmongoc's copy of the RFC 3454 tables.

TLS uses, as dependencies (no C): rustls (Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT), rustls-webpki (ISC)
and rustls-pki-types (MIT OR Apache-2.0) (https://github.com/rustls), the graviola crypto
library and its rustls provider rustls-graviola (https://github.com/ctz/graviola; Apache-2.0
OR ISC OR MIT-0; Rust with inline assembly, parts of it derived from s2n-bignum, Apache-2.0
OR ISC OR MIT-0), and for the key-file loader the RustCrypto crates pkcs8, pkcs5, spki, der,
aes, des, cbc, scrypt, salsa20 and pbkdf2 (https://github.com/RustCrypto; MIT OR Apache-2.0).
OCSP uses the RustCrypto crates x509-cert, x509-ocsp, der, spki and const-oid (Apache-2.0 OR
MIT), flagset (Apache-2.0) and sha1 (above).
Logging fingerprints use hmac and sha2 (above).
Wire compression uses, as dependencies (pure Rust): flate2 (https://github.com/rust-lang/flate2-rs;
MIT OR Apache-2.0) with miniz_oxide (https://github.com/Frommi/miniz_oxide; MIT OR Zlib OR
Apache-2.0), adler2 (0BSD OR MIT OR Apache-2.0), simd-adler32 (https://github.com/mcountryman/
simd-adler32; MIT) and crc32fast (MIT OR Apache-2.0); ruzstd (https://github.com/KillingSpark/
zstd-rs; MIT); snap (https://github.com/BurntSushi/rust-snappy; BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2011 The
Snappy-Rust Authors and Copyright 2016 Andrew Gallant).

